{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775379059-6OS3CU9YT7NmCi0CfVMc","role":"assistant","created":1775379061,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me identify when the Korean War started. The Korean War started in June 1950. The US fiscal year runs from October 1 to September 30. So the Korean War started in FY 1951 (which started October 1, 1950).\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The Korean War started on June 25, 1950. The US fiscal year 1950 runs from October 1, 1949 to September 30, 1950. So the Korean War started in FY 1950 (actually in the last month of FY 1950).\n\nBut since we're looking at the fiscal year \"during which the Korean War started\", this would be FY 1950 (the fiscal year that included June 1950).\n\nNow let me look at the treasury bulletin to find the data for Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance transfers.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8dfd222370044167bfa14df3","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"cat /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_02_page_25.txt | head -100"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
