ared to the overall budget.\n\nI'll calculate the compound annual growth rate using the precise values of 0.4 for FY1947 and 3.6 for FY1950. I'll need to verify the exact number of years between these fiscal periods to ensure an accurate calculation.\n\nFor the number of years, I'll count from mid-1947 to mid-1950, which gives me 3 years. However, I'm uncertain whether I should use 2 or 3 years, as fiscal year calculations can be tricky. I'll use Python to precisely determine the exact year difference.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_b39630aeb4d140a9844c6652","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Korean War started June 25, 1950\n# US Federal Fiscal Year runs July 1 to June 30\n# FY 1950 = July 1, 1949 to June 30, 1950\n# So the Korean War started in FY 1950\n\n# From the table, we need:\n# FY 1947: Transfers to F.O.A. and S.I. Trust Fund = .4 (million)\n# FY 1950: Transfers to F.O.A. and S.I. Trust Fund = 3.6 (million)\n\n# FY 1947 runs from July 1, 1946 to June 30, 1947\n# FY 1950 runs from July 1, 1949 to June 30, 1950\n\n# The time period is from FY 1947 to FY 1950\n# Number of years = 3 (from end of FY1947 to end of FY1950, or 1947 to 1950)\n\n# CAGR = (Ending Value / Beginning Value)^(1/n) - 1\n# Where n = number of years\n\nstart_value = 0.4  # million dollars in FY 1947\nend_value = 3.6    # million dollars in FY 1950\nn = 3  # years from FY1947 to FY1950\n\ncagr = (end_value / start_value) ** (1/n) - 1\ncagr_percent = cagr * 100\n\nprint(f\"Start value (FY 1947): ${start_value} million\")\nprint(f\"End value (FY 1950): ${end_value} million\")\nprint(f\"Number of years: {n}\")\nprint(f\"CAGR: {cagr}\")\nprint(f\"CAGR percent: {cagr_percent:.2f}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
